E('michael faraday|faraday', 'Michael Faraday was an English scientist who pioneered electricity and magnetism.', 'He lived from 1791 to 1867.', 'He discovered electromagnetic induction in 1831.', 'This principle powers electric generators and transformers.', 'He invented an early electric motor.', 'He had little formal schooling and began as a bookbinder’s apprentice.', 'He started the Royal Institution Christmas Lectures for young people.')
E('james clerk maxwell|maxwell', 'James Clerk Maxwell was a Scottish physicist.', 'He lived from 1831 to 1879.', 'His equations unified electricity, magnetism and light.', 'He showed light is an electromagnetic wave.', 'He took the first colour photograph in 1861.', 'Einstein kept his picture on his study wall.')
E('niels bohr|bohr', 'Niels Bohr was a Danish physicist who shaped our understanding of the atom.', 'He lived from 1885 to 1962.', 'His model put electrons in fixed orbits around the nucleus.', 'He won the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1922.', 'He had famous debates with Einstein about quantum theory.', 'He escaped Nazi-occupied Denmark in 1943.')
E('ernest rutherford|rutherford', 'Ernest Rutherford was a New Zealand-born physicist, the father of nuclear physics.', 'He lived from 1871 to 1937.', 'He discovered that atoms have a small, dense nucleus.', 'His gold foil experiment showed most of an atom is empty space.', 'He won the Nobel Prize in Chemistry in 1908.', 'His team first split the atom in 1932.')
E('richard feynman|feynman', 'Richard Feynman was an American theoretical physicist.', 'He lived from 1918 to 1988.', 'He won the 1965 Nobel Prize for work on quantum electrodynamics.', 'He invented Feynman diagrams.', 'He worked on the Manhattan Project.', 'He showed why the Challenger shuttle failed using a glass of ice water.', 'He was famous as a brilliant teacher and storyteller.')
E('hypatia', 'Hypatia was a mathematician, astronomer and philosopher in Alexandria.', 'She lived from about 355 to 415.', 'She taught philosophy and mathematics.', 'She is one of the first women mathematicians whose life is well recorded.', 'She was murdered by a Christian mob in 415.', 'She became a symbol of learning and reason.')
E('al-khwarizmi|al khwarizmi|algebra', 'Al-Khwarizmi was a Persian mathematician of the Islamic Golden Age.', 'He lived from about 780 to 850, working in Baghdad’s House of Wisdom.', 'His book on equations gave us the word “algebra”.', 'The word “algorithm” comes from his name.', 'He helped spread Hindu-Arabic numerals.', 'He is often called the father of algebra.')
E('ibn sina|avicenna', 'Ibn Sina, known in Europe as Avicenna, was a Persian physician and philosopher.', 'He lived from about 980 to 1037.', 'He wrote The Canon of Medicine.', 'It was a standard medical textbook in Europe for centuries.', 'He wrote on philosophy, astronomy and music too.', 'He is one of the most influential thinkers of the Islamic Golden Age.')
E('hippocrates|hippocratic oath', 'Hippocrates was an ancient Greek physician, called the father of medicine.', 'He lived from about 460 to 370 BC.', 'He taught that diseases have natural causes, not divine ones.', 'The Hippocratic Oath, an ethical code for doctors, is named after him.', 'Its principle is often summarised as “first, do no harm”.')
E('alfred nobel|nobel prize|nobel', 'Alfred Nobel was a Swedish chemist and inventor who founded the Nobel Prizes.', 'He lived from 1833 to 1896; the first prizes were awarded in 1901.', 'He invented dynamite in 1867.', 'A newspaper mistakenly printed his obituary, calling him a “merchant of death”.', 'He left his fortune to fund prizes for those who benefit humanity.', 'Prizes are given in physics, chemistry, medicine, literature and peace; economics was added later.')
E('carl sagan|sagan|pale blue dot', 'Carl Sagan was an American astronomer and science communicator.', 'He lived from 1934 to 1996.', 'He presented the TV series Cosmos in 1980.', 'He helped design the Voyager Golden Records.', 'He wrote about the “Pale Blue Dot” photo of Earth.', 'He made astronomy exciting for millions.')
E('jane goodall|goodall', 'Jane Goodall is an English primatologist famous for studying chimpanzees.', 'She was born in 1934 and began her research in Tanzania in 1960.', 'She discovered that chimpanzees make and use tools.', 'She showed they have personalities and complex social lives.', 'She founded the Jane Goodall Institute.', 'She became a global voice for conservation.')
E('david attenborough|attenborough', 'Sir David Attenborough is an English broadcaster and naturalist.', 'He was born in 1926.', 'He has made nature documentaries for over 70 years.', 'His series include Life on Earth, Planet Earth and Blue Planet.', 'He is a leading voice on climate and conservation.', 'Several species are named after him.')
E('rachel carson|silent spring', 'Rachel Carson was an American marine biologist and writer.', 'She lived from 1907 to 1964.', 'Her book Silent Spring (1962) warned about pesticides like DDT.', 'It helped launch the modern environmental movement.', 'It led to a US ban on DDT for farm use in 1972.')
E('grace hopper', 'Grace Hopper was an American computer scientist and navy rear admiral.', 'She lived from 1906 to 1992.', 'She developed one of the first compilers.', 'She helped create the programming language COBOL.', 'She popularised the term “bug” after a moth was found in a computer.', 'She was nicknamed “Amazing Grace”.')
E('katherine johnson|hidden figures', 'Katherine Johnson was an American mathematician at NASA.', 'She lived from 1918 to 2020.', 'She calculated flight paths for early US space missions.', 'John Glenn asked her personally to check the computer’s numbers before his 1962 orbit.', 'She worked on the Apollo 11 mission.', 'The film Hidden Figures tells her story.')
E('steve jobs|iphone', 'Steve Jobs was an American entrepreneur who co-founded Apple.', 'He lived from 1955 to 2011.', 'He founded Apple with Steve Wozniak in 1976.', 'He was forced out in 1985 and returned in 1997.', 'He launched the iPod, iPhone and iPad.', 'He also led Pixar Animation Studios.', 'He was famous for his product launches in a black turtleneck.')
E('bill gates|microsoft', 'Bill Gates is an American businessman who co-founded Microsoft.', 'He was born in 1955 and founded Microsoft with Paul Allen in 1975.', 'Microsoft’s Windows became the dominant PC operating system.', 'He was the world’s richest person for many years.', 'He co-founded a major charitable foundation focused on global health.')
E('mark zuckerberg|facebook', 'Mark Zuckerberg is an American businessman who co-founded Facebook.', 'He was born in 1984 and launched Facebook in 2004.', 'He started it as a student at Harvard.', 'The company renamed itself Meta in 2021.', 'It also owns Instagram and WhatsApp.')
E('elon musk|spacex', 'Elon Musk is a businessman known for leading SpaceX and Tesla.', 'He was born in South Africa in 1971.', 'SpaceX was founded in 2002 and developed reusable rockets.', 'He led the electric car company Tesla.', 'He bought Twitter in 2022 and renamed it X.', 'He is a prominent and polarising public figure.')
E('jeff bezos|amazon company', 'Jeff Bezos is an American businessman who founded Amazon.', 'He was born in 1964 and founded Amazon in 1994.', 'Amazon began as an online bookshop.', 'It grew into one of the world’s largest companies.', 'He founded the space company Blue Origin.')
E('hedy lamarr', 'Hedy Lamarr was an Austrian-American film star and inventor.', 'She lived from 1914 to 2000.', 'She was a major Hollywood star in the 1930s and 1940s.', 'She co-invented a frequency-hopping system to stop torpedoes being jammed.', 'Ideas like it later helped make Wi-Fi and Bluetooth possible.')
E('galen', 'Galen was a Greek physician in the Roman Empire.', 'He lived from about AD 129 to 216.', 'He was physician to emperors, including Marcus Aurelius.', 'He dissected animals to study anatomy.', 'His ideas dominated medicine for over a thousand years, mistakes included.')
E('andreas vesalius|vesalius', 'Andreas Vesalius was a Flemish anatomist, the founder of modern anatomy.', 'He lived from 1514 to 1564.', 'His book On the Fabric of the Human Body appeared in 1543.', 'He corrected many of Galen’s errors through dissection.', 'Its illustrations were stunningly accurate.')
E('william harvey', 'William Harvey was an English physician.', 'He lived from 1578 to 1657.', 'He discovered that blood circulates around the body, pumped by the heart.', 'He published his findings in 1628.', 'Many doctors at first rejected his idea.')
E('carl linnaeus|linnaeus', 'Carl Linnaeus was a Swedish botanist who created the modern system for naming living things.', 'He lived from 1707 to 1778.', 'He gave each species a two-part Latin name, like Homo sapiens.', 'This is called binomial nomenclature.', 'He is called the father of taxonomy.')
E('lavoisier|antoine lavoisier', 'Antoine Lavoisier was a French chemist, the father of modern chemistry.', 'He lived from 1743 to 1794.', 'He named oxygen and hydrogen.', 'He showed that mass is conserved in chemical reactions.', 'He was guillotined during the French Revolution because he had been a tax collector.')
E('joseph lister|lister|antiseptic', 'Joseph Lister was a British surgeon who pioneered antiseptic surgery.', 'He lived from 1827 to 1912.', 'He used carbolic acid to clean wounds and instruments.', 'This sharply reduced deaths after surgery.', 'The mouthwash Listerine is named after him.')
E('max planck|planck', 'Max Planck was a German physicist, the founder of quantum theory.', 'He lived from 1858 to 1947.', 'In 1900 he proposed that energy comes in small packets, or quanta.', 'He won the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1918.', 'Planck’s constant is one of the fundamental numbers of physics.')
E('heisenberg|werner heisenberg|uncertainty principle', 'Werner Heisenberg was a German physicist and a founder of quantum mechanics.', 'He lived from 1901 to 1976.', 'He formulated the uncertainty principle in 1927.', 'It says you cannot know a particle’s exact position and momentum at the same time.', 'He won the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1932.')
E('schrodinger|schrödinger|schrodingers cat|schrödinger’s cat', 'Erwin Schrödinger was an Austrian physicist, a founder of quantum mechanics.', 'He lived from 1887 to 1961.', 'His equation describes how quantum systems change.', 'His “cat” thought experiment imagined a cat both alive and dead until observed.', 'He meant it to show how strange quantum theory is.', 'He won the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1933.')
E('robert hooke|hooke', 'Robert Hooke was an English scientist and polymath.', 'He lived from 1635 to 1703.', 'He coined the word “cell” after looking at cork through a microscope.', 'His book Micrographia appeared in 1665.', 'He described the law of elasticity, Hooke’s law.', 'He had a bitter rivalry with Isaac Newton.')
E('antonie van leeuwenhoek|leeuwenhoek|microscope', 'Antonie van Leeuwenhoek was a Dutch scientist, the father of microbiology.', 'He lived from 1632 to 1723.', 'He built his own powerful microscopes.', 'He was the first to see bacteria and single-celled organisms, which he called “animalcules”.', 'He had no university training.')
